# Your corpus. Real text, often large, and not something to push.
data/*
# ...except the two small files A05b commits: where the corpus came from, and (Wikipedia) the article list.
!data/README.md
!data/SOURCE.md
!data/titles.txt

# Saved arrays. Regenerate them, do not commit them.
*.npy

# ...except these two. A05 embeds once and saves; A06 builds on exactly those
# vectors, and I re-run your numbers against them, so they are part of the
# deliverable rather than a build artifact.
!embed/vecs.npy
!embed/words.npy

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Secrets. The guard blocks these at commit time as well; this is belt and braces.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

.DS_Store
!.env.example
secrets.json
students_keys.csv
openrouter_keys.csv
